.vercel

# Build Outputs
.next/
.next-*/
out/
build
dist


# Debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Local editor state. `.vscode/settings.json` in this repo is one developer's
# window tinting (`workbench.colorCustomizations`) — a personal preference, not
# shared project configuration. Commit a shared config deliberately if one is
# ever wanted; do not let this one ride along.
.vscode/

# Stray archives. `apps/api/src/srccccccc.zip` — 95 KB of zipped source — was
# committed once because nothing stopped it, and it sat inside the NestJS
# compile root. This rule is why it cannot happen again.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# COMMERCIAL FONT BINARIES — deliberately NOT in this repository.
#
# Yekan Bakh is all-rights-reserved software whose own embedded licence record
# says "To use this font, it is necessary to obtain the license from
# www.fontiran.com", and this project makes no claim to hold that licence. Its
# .woff2 files are therefore excluded from version control while
# `packages/ui/fonts/README.md` — which IS committed — records the exact files,
# their SHA-256 hashes, the licence position and where they must be placed.
#
# CONSEQUENCE: none for the build. The typeface is layered. `Vazirmatn`
# (SIL OFL 1.1) is committed under `packages/ui/fonts/vazirmatn/` and is what
# `next/font/local` loads in both root layouts, so a fresh clone builds and
# renders correct Persian with no licensed asset present. Yekan Bakh is layered
# on top by plain `@font-face` rules pointing at `/fonts/*.woff2` in each app's
# `public/fonts/` — a root-relative URL the bundler never resolves, so absent
# files cost a 404 and nothing more. A licensee drops the four files in and the
# brand face appears with no code change.
#
# The first pattern is NOT recursive: `*` does not cross `/`, so it catches
# `packages/ui/fonts/YekanBakh-*.woff2` while leaving the committed
# `packages/ui/fonts/vazirmatn/*.woff2` alone. That is load-bearing.
packages/ui/fonts/*.woff2
apps/*/public/fonts/

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
